| Existing result | What it supports |
|---|---|
| Constructed witnesses, including profitable occupancy and swap examples | Existence and causal explanation within the declared model. Positive interaction in the other witnesses does not automatically imply a profitable joint move. |
| Qualifying coalitions at 30/30 anchors; median best-coalition gain 9.118% | Repeated occurrence in one tested world, relative to the nearest-eligible carrier. This is neither independent-date prevalence nor gain above unilateral convergence. |
| +6.359% pooled EE over converged unilateral selection, across 20 anchors in four TRAIN worlds | Demonstrated additional value from a bounded coalition search starting at those unilateral fixed points. No deadline or learned policy was involved. |
| Positive gains under 18 circuit-cost combinations | The already-selected assignments retain their advantage when those energy terms are rescored. This does not test reoptimised policies or other physical assumptions. |

The latter three distinctions come directly from [PREVALENCE](/home/sat/mcrl-v023-codex-audits/parallel-20260909/PREVALENCE-CODEX-2026-09-09.md:21), [ORACLE](/home/sat/mcrl-v023-codex-audits/parallel-20260909/ORACLE-CODEX-2026-09-09.md:54), and the [controller findings](/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDINGS-AFTERNOON-2026-09-09.md).

The oracle result is not a mathematical ceiling. Its comparator is a local fixed point reached by one specified unilateral procedure, under its objective and constraints. It is not the best outcome obtainable by every unilateral search strategy, and it is not a certified global pooled-EE optimum. The useful claim is that coordinated moves improve these certified local endpoints.

This mechanism deserves the remaining effort because its decisive uncertainty is identifiable: whether the modelling and control assumptions make it relevant beyond these examples. The learned-controller programme still has unresolved targets, representation, decision quality, timing and independent evaluation. Finishing all of that is a new project, not the last repair before the present paper.

**1. Retire the three-component conjunction as the primary design.** Its statistical formulation can be coherent while its scientific purpose is wrong.

The contract’s intervention is specifically informative-versus-neutral **source training**, with all heads retained. Even successful FULL-minus-DROP results would establish the usefulness of three particular training routes in this construction. They would not establish three independent physical contributions or the necessity of this architecture. A useful system with redundant routes can fail the conjunction; a carefully arranged decomposition can make all three routes appear indispensable. That makes the conjunction a poor definition of whether the research succeeded. [Contract, §C3–C6](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-codex-ws-engine/.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md)

The +664% and +6.36% figures do **not** mathematically prove that three +0.5% marginals are impossible. They have different denominators and the ablation effects need not partition either gain. Nor is 6.36% intrinsically trivial. What the proportions reveal is a comparator problem: enormous gains are available by replacing a geometry-only carrier with exact optimisation before learning enters the story. The paper must explain the incremental contribution after a competent baseline, not borrow the carrier’s weakness to make the architecture look consequential.

The decomposition also no longer matches the clearest mechanism. A threshold on aggregate occupancy is naturally a beam-level property. The reported higher-order remainder exceeds its descriptive materiality threshold on 38.5% of the tested coalitions of size at least three. That rejects an exact pairwise-only account on this corpus; it does not imply that a larger neural model is necessary. A simple nonlinear occupancy rule can represent high-order dependence. [COALGEN](/home/sat/mcrl-v023-codex-audits/parallel-20260909/COALGEN-CODEX-2026-09-09.md:28)

Use an ordered claim structure: establish the mechanism, establish its occurrence in explicitly named scenarios, then test a practical method for exploiting it. Component ablations belong under that last claim if they answer a real explanatory question. The paper should survive a zero marginal from C1 or C2.

**3. Stop the following work now.**

- **Stop preparing the full three-route success panel.** Six arms and many learner seeds do not make sense before one useful learned decision procedure exists. One evaluated independent ephemeris date cannot support the intended generalisation claim. The approximately 142 free dates are not automatically insufficient for every possible study, but the original approximately 160-date power argument cannot simply be carried over. Preserve them until the research question is settled.
- **Stop expanding the corpus toward 51,000–93,000 labels because a curve extrapolates to 60% exact-best selection.** That target is not the paper’s endpoint. At the largest measured point, the head still loses to zero interaction on regret and realised EE; its EE is 10.3098 versus 10.3178 Mbit/J. More accurate predictions have not yet produced a better decision rule. The size-three-plus result is especially instructive: better exact-best frequency coexists with worse regret and EE. [CURVE](/home/sat/mcrl-v023-codex-audits/parallel-20260909/CURVE-CODEX-2026-09-09.md:28)
- **Stop rebuilding C1 and C2 merely to preserve the three-component story.** Their invalid measurements must be excluded. Repairing two additional learned surrogates is justified only if the selected scientific question needs them. The mechanism study does not. The curve experiment itself uses exact C1, so it is not evidence that the complete three-component system is approaching validity. [C1C2](/home/sat/mcrl-v023-codex-audits/parallel-20260909/C1C2-CODEX-2026-09-09.md), [CURVE protocol](/home/sat/mcrl-v023-codex-audits/parallel-20260909/CURVE-CODEX-2026-09-09.md)
- **Stop treating modest timeout increases or faster final certification as the solution to the unilateral baseline.** The profiling report finds late winners requiring 41–86 improving iterations; its longest uncensored run takes 1,213 seconds. The tail is not just time spent proving that an already-found winner is best. Keep offline local-optimum certification for scientific diagnosis; use a separately declared anytime comparator for operational evaluation. [CERTPROFILE](/home/sat/mcrl-v023-codex-audits/parallel-20260909/CERTPROFILE-CODEX-2026-09-09.md:17)
- **Stop further sweeps of the disputed circuit constant as a rescue strategy.** The fixed-assignment sensitivity already answers whether that constant creates the observed sign. Additional points do not answer whether the occupancy-dependent control law is an appropriate model.
- **Stop broad defect adjudication and gate reconstruction as the project’s default activity.** There is already enough evidence to quarantine the old learned results. Repair and verify only the paths required for the newly selected result. More assurance about an abandoned claim is not progress toward a publishable one.

The learning curve does contain a legitimate, limited measurement of learning. It does not rescue the end-to-end component claim. “Still improving” is a diagnosis, not a go decision.

**4. The smallest credible publication is a short, explicitly exploratory simulation-mechanism paper.** A suitable scope is *Occupancy thresholds and coordinated association changes under rate-target power control in a LEO handover model*.

Its central result would be: under the specified multiplexing, power-control and mode-selection rules, service and energy can be complementary across users; coordinated changes can preserve service and improve the objective when their constituent individual changes do not. The zero-interference occupancy construction and the service-preserving swap are sufficient to make that result concrete. The bounded oracle experiment supplies an illustrative magnitude above a stronger local baseline. The prevalence census supplies evidence that the mechanism occurs repeatedly outside the hand-built examples.

The +6.359% must remain a descriptive result for the stated panel. The 30/30 must remain within-world occurrence. The increase from 1,939 to 1,957 in summed served counts is useful, but it does not establish all three contracted QoS non-inferiority conditions: “served” here requires positive decoding time, not attainment of the rate target or uninterrupted service. No number of anchors or learner seeds turns the one completed ephemeris date into independent date replication. [ORACLE](/home/sat/mcrl-v023-codex-audits/parallel-20260909/ORACLE-CODEX-2026-09-09.md:7), [PSI-WITNESS service definition](/home/sat/mcrl-v023-codex-audits/parallel-20260909/PSI-WITNESS-CODEX-2026-09-09.md:23)

There is also a publication-status distinction. The controller’s record explicitly says these diagnostics may not enter the paper or support a claim. The scientific minimum exists, but the present seal does not authorise publishing it as a successful evaluation. A pivot requires an explicit new study declaration and honest exploratory provenance. It must leave the original learned conjunction unestablished rather than retroactively pronounce it successful.

The weakest point under review is **model relevance**, ahead of sample size for this narrow existence claim. A reviewer can ask: “Does consolidation solve an unavoidable association problem, or compensate for your chosen power-control and back-off policy?” The witness demonstrates that loading a beam makes the controller allocate enough power to permit a transmitted mode. That is a property of this control-and-physics combination, not a universal physical law about loading satellites. Robustness to circuit accounting does not answer that objection. The already-recorded beamwidth sensitivity makes this distinction more consequential. [Controller findings, §2](/home/sat/mcrl-records/decisions/V025-CONTROLLER-FINDINGS-AFTERNOON-2026-09-09.md)

A credible short submission is available. A broad claim of deployable superiority, general prevalence or literature novelty is not established by these records.

**5. The frame missing from the programme is the price of the lower-level control rule.** The contract already distinguishes offline headroom from operational performance and already permits acceleration claims. Rediscovering those distinctions is useful housekeeping, but it is not a new research direction. [Contract amendment v1.2](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-codex-ws-engine/.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1.2-AMENDMENT-2026-09-09.md)

The deeper alternative is to ask whether the occupancy-induced blackout should exist in the first place. Consider a service-aware power/mode policy that can allocate enough power for a feasible transmitted mode without requiring two additional users to arrive. Compare that policy with the existing rate-target/back-off law under the same physical constraints and explicit service obligations. This is a new scientific intervention, not a permissible silent change to the sealed benchmark. If much of the coordination gain disappears, the contribution becomes a diagnosis of the control law and its remedy. That could be more useful than teaching three networks to compensate for it. I have not seen that comparison in the supplied record.

Three changes of viewpoint follow:

- **Decision unit:** choose beam occupancy patterns and complete user bundles, then resolve individual assignments. The physical mechanism suggests these units directly. A deterministic occupancy-aware coalition proposer with exact validation is the comparator a learned coordinator should have to beat.
- **Objective:** examine minimum energy for an explicitly specified delivered-service obligation, alongside the existing pooled-EE ratio. This would reveal whether the gain represents cheaper adequate service or movement along a throughput–energy tradeoff. The 50 Mbit/s power-control setpoint must not silently become a demonstrated service guarantee.
- **Operational claim:** measure useful validated improvement available by ten seconds against an anytime unilateral method and the simple mechanism-aware proposer. Count fallback outcomes and all decision work. If learning eventually wins, ask whether it reduces expensive evaluations or finds better candidates sooner. Predicting an exact score after paying to evaluate every candidate provides no automatic acceleration benefit.

If a learned contribution is mandatory, first consider learning to accelerate the expensive unilateral search itself. That targets the largest demonstrated improvement over the carrier and the clearest operational bottleneck. The existing figures do not establish that learning can recover that gain cheaply; they identify a more consequential approximation problem than insisting that every route earns its own half percent.

My next allocation would be to write the conditional mechanism argument and resolve its central modelling objection. I would permit a learning continuation only after naming an outcome-based advantage over an appropriate simple controller that the continuation is designed to establish. Another upward segment of prediction accuracy would not meet that condition.
19:**Two. The reason it loses is structural, not statistical.** `COALGEN` measured `|R3| > 1e-3` on **38.50 %** of 5,003 coalitions of size ≥ 3. The deployed model is a pairwise-conditioned interaction head. That is a measured misspecification, not a suspicion. Buying the extrapolated 51,000–93,000 labels buys data for a model form that has been proven unable to represent the target on more than a third of the support. And the extrapolation itself is a log-linear fit through three points, to a 60 %-exact-best target that the diagnostic chose for itself, extended 6–11× beyond observed range. `CURVE` says this plainly and the controller should take it at its word.
23:Now stack the work required to make the learner a contribution: exact C1/C2 labels replacing the proxy path, a feature interface that resolves the collisions, an interaction model that is not pairwise, a new corpus at ~10× scale, retraining, then the 10 s budget question, then a panel that (see Frame D) cannot currently be allocated. That is not the remainder of this project. That is the next one.
35:**It decomposes the wrong thing.** C1/C2/C3 is a decomposition of the *learner's architecture*. The value ladder in the physics is: geometry-only carrier → exact joint objective evaluation of single-user moves → multi-user coordination. That is a decomposition you can measure exactly, today, with no learner and no ablation arms. The project has been treating an engineering module boundary as if it were a scientific one.
41:**The proportions make the conjunction look worse than it is, and the +664 % is not usable.** `C1C2` §6 verified the baseline: across 6,000 cases the `nearest-eligible` carrier action was the best action *even within the already-truncated 9-item shortlist* **49 times — 0.817 %**, mean rank 8.255 of 9. The +664 % is the distance from a geometry-only, near-worst-ranked reference to an exact joint optimiser. Publishing it as a headline will read as inflation and will cost credibility on the +6.36 % that is the actual result. Report it once, with the rank statistics attached, and never as an achievement.
57:5. **The CH5 sweep panels as currently framed** (70.6 projected core-hours, 8 named arm series). Panel F is explicitly degenerate — all arm curves coincide by construction, and the report says so. The arm-curve framing plots unvalidated learned arms. Keep panel B (circuit power 0.1 / 0.338 / 1.0 W) and panel E (architecture siblings) as **physics** sensitivities for the mechanism claim; drop the arm decomposition from all of them.
73:1. **Mechanism.** Under a rate target with equal-airtime TDM and ACM, raising beam occupancy enlarges back-off room so that a lower-order mode clears its SINR threshold; adding load to a beam can make it servable. Four constructive witnesses in the production scoring path with exact score identities, and a reuse-colour control that drives Ψ to −5.9e−6 bits and isolates interference as necessary in mechanism 1.
100:Everything in this project is decomposed per-user and per-anchor, credited to C1/C2/C3. But the measured mechanism is a property of a **beam**: occupancy 1 or 2 is a transmitter burning fixed power for nothing, occupancy ≥ 3 activates a servable mode. Sixty-one percent of active beam-anchor incidences are in that wasteful regime. The natural policy object is not a coalition — it is a rule: *no beam operates below occupancy 3; consolidate or empty.*
104:- If a hand-written occupancy floor captures most of the headroom, that is a **better paper** than a neural coordinator — a physically motivated, deployable, sub-millisecond rule that beats an exhaustive unilateral optimiser — and it retires the learner question entirely.
111:Pooled EE = ΣB/ΣE with QoS as non-inferiority *guards*. The load-balancing mechanism firing at 0 of 30 anchors should be read as information about the objective, not only about the physics: as posed, it has no per-user rate or fairness term with teeth, so the optimiser has no reason to spread load ever. A referee in this area will ask what consolidation does to worst-decile user rate and to handover churn, and "the guard was satisfied" is a weaker answer than a reported frontier. Consider making QoS an **outcome**: report the (pooled EE, worst-decile rate) frontier. Consolidation that improves both is a substantially stronger claim than consolidation that improves one subject to not-degrading the other — and the served counts (1,957 vs 1,939, and 30/30 anchors with served counts flat or rising) suggest you may already have the stronger version and are reporting the weaker one.
115:The project has been asking "does coordination beat the exhaustive unilateral optimum," which is a theory question you have now answered: yes, by 6.36 %, and the optimum costs 1,213 s. The question the 10 s budget actually supports is a **deployability** question, and it wants a different comparator set: carrier default; one-pass greedy unilateral within 10 s; occupancy-floor heuristic within 10 s; oracle. That frame uses `CERTPROFILE` as a load-bearing result rather than an obstacle, needs no learner, and is where the remaining headroom in the *paper* lives.
131:Tomorrow: (1) run the occupancy-floor heuristic against the oracle catalogue — Frame A; (2) run ORACLE over ~30 dates to put an interval on +6.36 % — Q4's weak point. Both are learner-free, both are hours not days, and between them they determine whether the paper's headline is "a simple physical rule captures most of a 6 % coordination headroom" or "a 6 % coordination headroom exists that neither exhaustive search nor a learned head can reach."

